# Ground-state QM/MM MD across a COVALENT QM/MM boundary (see the
# frontier_scheme section of README.md): alanine dipeptide with AMBER-14,
# QM = the C-terminal amide, so the partition cuts the ALA C-CA bond and the
# MM host charge is redistributed by frontier_scheme=rcd.
# qmmm(qm_atoms=...) is the one definition of the QM region (0-based PDB
# order); the QM molecule, link hydrogen included, is built from it.
# velocity=zero keeps the two steps reproducible.  Requires OpenMM.
rks/bhhlyp/6-31g md(nstep=2,dt=0.5,velocity=zero,ensemble=nve)
qmmm(forcefield_files="amber14-all.xml",qm_atoms="8,9,16,17,18",frontier_scheme=rcd,cutoff=NoCutoff)
geom="ala.pdb"
